results.summary:
R7 pass-2 DFM, assembly and fabrication-package review, read-only. The board is unchanged (SHA-256 03fe7572…6d54) and tools/check.sh exits 0. Full report: m3_design/assembly_review/sources/r7_review/pass2_dfm.md.

What checks out:
- Every new footprint matches its maker drawing: MAX-F10S copper, mask and T-paste (IM Fig. 25/26), E22 against the EBYTE ch. 3 drawing, ESD103 against TSLP-2-20 Fig. 14 (except the documented per-pad mask), LQG15 §11.1, BLM18K §10-1, and the Kinghelm SMA drawing.
- Courtyards enclose pads and paste. The new lands match JLC/EasyEDA by pad number. EasyEDA's silkscreen and 3D origin confirm the SMA body points −y, so CPL rotation 0 is right.
- jlc_orient --verify-cpl passes (92 top + 119 bottom rows, 8 placement-only). fab_manifest is OK.
- export_fab regenerated into scratch gives an identical BOM and CPL, and identical Gerbers, drill and job files apart from timestamps. Saved zone fills are current.
- The job file carries the JLC041611-7628 stackup. The tab windows match ORDERING within 0.03 mm. The 90 hidden designators equal the M3_R7 list. Text is ≥ 1.0 mm.
- Live JLC API (2026-10-16 05:48Z): every line is in stock for 5 boards except the documented U4 consignment. $110.93 per board with 52 extended codes meets M3.

Findings: Critical 0, Major 1, Minor 10.
- **Major (DFM-01):** R100.1 has an open via hole in its soldered pad (M2). It was inherited from R6 and neither the gate nor ORDERING catches it.
- **Minor:**
  - paste on the DNP shunt pads;
  - the unsupported forward 50 mm, although the forward short edge has compliant tab windows;
  - the left tab is 1.83 mm from J3, under JLC's 2 mm connector keep-out;
  - the ESD diodes are 0.50 mm from the hand-soldered SMA centre pads;
  - the SMA legs are heavily heat-sunk (vias at a 0.20 mm gap);
  - U30's T-paste prints over two GND vias;
  - the LS120 reflow rating is now verified at 250 °C max (closes R7P1-13);
  - the MAX-F10S 245 °C peak equals JLC's upper bound, and its TAL is not in the remarks;
  - antenna label and designator nits;
  - duplicate LCSC codes on separate BOM lines.

verdicts.recommended_fix:
No board change. Documentation fixes:

1. Rewrite VEHICLE.md l.39 for R7 now:
   - board 118 mm (46 × 118, M3-ASSY-R7);
   - five standoffs at (4,4), (42.3,4), (4,64), (4,114.4), (42,114.4);
   - SMA jacks on the aft edge, 9.5 mm overhang plus about 16 mm mated plug;
   - battery-lead and RG316 coax-loop zone about 41 mm aft of the board, kept off the camera-shroud side between joint +4 and +47;
   - slack about 59–71 mm;
   - board position pending the shroud measurement.
   Commit it in the parent repo, per the parent CLAUDE.md rule.
2. Add a short "Bay stack and orientation" line to M3_R7.md: y=0 is the aft edge with J30/J31 pointing aft; J1 is at the forward end (y ≈ 110.4), so the battery leads run the board's length; cross-reference ORDERING §7.
3. In REQUIREMENTS l.86, replace "about 70 mm below the coupler's forward end ± 3 mm" with "aft edge at joint ≥ +76 (coax loops on the side away from the shroud) or ≥ +88 (loops forward of the shroud), fixed after the Onshape shroud measurement".

These are cheap, proportionate documentation edits; none of them blocks the PCB order.
(a) Update the VEHICLE.md stack row to R7 and keep it concise, per the project-docs-concise rule:
- board 46 × 118 mm, with the SMA jacks on the aft edge (9.5 mm overhang plus straight plugs);
- J1's entry faces forward, so the battery leads run the board's length;
- five holes at (4, 4), (42.3, 4), (4, 64), (4, 114.4) and (42, 114.4);
- a coax loop zone of ~41-48 mm in place of the 15 mm lead zone;
- slack ~52-71 mm, depending on shroud clearance;
- point to ORDERING §7 for the sled details.
Commit it in the top-level repo per CLAUDE.md.
(b) Add a two-line "bay stack and orientation" note to M3_R7.md that points to ORDERING l.5 and §7. Do not duplicate them.
(c) In REQUIREMENTS, replace the stale "70 mm below the coupler's forward end ± 3" with the derived constraint: aft edge ≥ battery-bay top + coax zone, about joint +76…+83, or about +88…+95 if the loops must clear the shroud entirely. Keep it marked open until the Onshape shroud measurement. Use a range rather than a single value, so that MECHANICAL-04's coax allocation can change it without another edit.
